      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T17:29:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a tilted band's column dips by the rim's exact R·sin θ\n\nThe leaning column of the reach laws stood each band's bottom one whole\nradius under its foot. Just above the upright tolerance of #938 an r 12\nholder 5 mm clear of a part read 12 mm lower and was convicted\nShankHit { part: true }: a cliff at 1e-9 rad that any commanded tilt\npaid.\n\nOne helper, verify::tilt_band::lean, now builds the column for every\nlaw that reads a leaning stack - reach (c), its mid-turn sweep (c3), the\nfixture band column (c2) and the tilted rapid (d2). The centre and\nradius are the sums they were; the z planes stand at the band's true\nlowest and highest points, foot -/+ R·sin θ (a unit vector square to the\naxis has a z part of at most sin θ, reached at the rim). An axis off\nunit length reads the larger sine, a zero or non-finite one the whole\nradius: never shallower than the band. Upright branches are untouched.\n\nVerdicts that move: tilted moves only, toward clean only, where the old\nextra depth was what met the material. tilt_tolerance.rs (#938) no\nlonger expects a holder 5 mm over the stock to convict at 1.01e-9 rad;\nit pins the conviction at 20 degrees, where the rim is in the stock.\nNo golden or posted output changes.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/tilt_band_dip.rs (clean at small tilts, a\nrim in the part convicts from 0.6 to 60 degrees, monotone across the\ntolerance, the mid-turn sweep) and the tilt_band unit tests (4000-case\ncontainment property, limits, the (c2) column). The posed capsule\nsweep's end caps keep the same cliff in the fixture verdict: #1305.\n\nFixes #1303\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
